\fs36 \cf0 Project Name: Ada Haskell Compiler (AHC)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Document Version:
\f1\b0  1.1 
\f0\b Date:
\f1\b0  July 2026\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Executive Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The 
\f0\b Ada Haskell Compiler (AHC)
\f1\b0  is a new, ground-up implementation of a Haskell compiler written entirely in Ada 2022. The objective is to create a highly reliable, formally verifiable, and robust compiler for the Haskell 2010 specification. By leveraging Ada's powerful type system, Design-by-Contract (DbC) features, and strict memory management, AHC aims to eliminate entire classes of bugs typical in compiler development (such as memory leaks, null pointer dereferences, and invariant violations during type inference).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Goals and Objectives\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compliance:
\f1\b0  Implement the Haskell 2010 Language Report specifications as faithfully as possible.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compiler Reliability:
\f1\b0  Utilize Ada 2022's advanced features (contracts, subtypes, variant records) to mathematically guarantee the internal consistency of the compiler's intermediate representations.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Maintainability:
\f1\b0  Create a highly readable and self-documenting compiler codebase using Ada's descriptive syntax.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Safety-Critical Functional Programming:
\f1\b0  Pave the way for functional programming to be adopted in high-integrity systems by providing a compiler toolchain built on high-integrity foundations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Scope\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 3.1. In-Scope\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Language Standard:
\f1\b0  Haskell 2010.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evaluation Model:
\f1\b0  Lazy evaluation (Call-by-need) and graph reduction.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Type System:
\f1\b0  Hindley-Milner type inference, Type Classes, and Monads as defined in Haskell 2010.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Standard Library:
\f1\b0  A core subset of the Haskell 2010 
\f2\fs26 Prelude
\f1\fs24  to ensure basic usability.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Code Generation:
\f1\b0  Compilation to a standard intermediate representation (e.g., LLVM IR or C) to leverage existing optimizers and backends.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ada Implementation:
\f1\b0  Strict adherence to Ada 2022 standards.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.2. Out-of-Scope\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 GHC Extensions:
\f1\b0  Advanced extensions like Template Haskell, Type Families, Multi-parameter type classes (unless strictly necessary), and Linear Types are deferred to future versions.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Garbage Collector Implementation:
\f1\b0  AHC will rely on an existing, proven C/C++ garbage collector (like the Boehm GC or GHC's RTS) linked during the final compilation phase, rather than writing a new GC in Ada for this initial release.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Interactive Environment (REPL):
\f1\b0  The initial focus is on a batch compiler (AOT), not a GHCi equivalent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Technical Requirements\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 4.1. Respecting Haskell 2010\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The compiler must correctly parse, type-check, and execute standard Haskell constructs:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Algebraic Data Types (ADTs):
\f1\b0  Correctly map Haskell ADTs into internal representations.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pattern Matching:
\f1\b0  Exhaustiveness checking and efficient compilation of complex nested patterns.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Type Classes:
\f1\b0  Resolution of dictionaries at compile-time.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Purity and Laziness:
\f1\b0  Ensure side-effects are strictly contained within the 
\f2\fs26 IO
\f1\fs24  Monad and thunks are correctly managed and updated upon evaluation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4.2. Utilizing Ada 2022\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The core differentiator of this compiler is 
\f3\i how
\f1\i0  it is built. The Ada 2022 standard will be utilized in the following ways:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Design by Contract (DbC):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f3\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f4 \uc0\u9702 
\f3 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pre/Post-conditions:
\f1\i0  Applied to critical functions like AST transformations and Type Unification. For example, 
\f2\fs26 Post => Type_Check'Result.Is_Valid
\f1\fs24  ensuring no invalid type nodes leak out of the inference engine.\
\ls5\ilvl1
\f3\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f4 \uc0\u9702 
\f3 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Type Invariants:
\f1\i0  Applied to Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) nodes to ensure tree integrity (e.g., ensuring a 
\f2\fs26 Let
\f1\fs24  binding always has at least one declaration).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Advanced Typing and Variant Records:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f5 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Haskell's AST and Core language will be modeled using Ada's variant records (discriminated records). This perfectly mirrors Algebraic Data Types in a memory-safe, strictly bounded way.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f3\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f4 \uc0\u9702 
\f3 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Subtypes:
\f1\i0  Extensive use of subtypes with dynamic predicates to catch boundary errors at compile-time or run-time of the compiler itself.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
